MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rows of the receipt were text only, hard to tell apart. Each row now
starts with the posting app's launcher icon (so the Budík icon overlays
apply) in a 6 dp keycap frame, or the notification's small icon tinted
like text for the system and apps without an icon. The time moves next
to the title; the app name is no longer shown, TalkBack reads it from
the icon. Icons are decoded on the background dispatcher once per
package and user and kept in a small LRU cache (48 entries of 26 dp),
so scrolling and swiping never wait for them.
